Bump russh from 0.64.1 to 0.65.1 (security fix).

russh < 0.65.1 runs the client's kex_done() callback with the key-exchange shared secret before
check_server_key() has accepted the server's host key (GHSA-9264-jvgf-6w2f, low). Litterbox uses
russh for its agent protocol server, not as an SSH client, and does not implement kex_done(), so
it is not reachable here; the bump clears the advisory and keeps the scanners quiet.

This is upstream's own Dependabot change (Gerharddc/Litterbox#217), unchanged: russh moves in
Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock, and two crates it no longer needs drop out. Drop this patch once
upstream ships a release with russh >= 0.65.1.

